IMPORT prelude

-- Health Insurance Act 1973 (Cth) -- who is an "eligible person" (s 3(1): "Australian resident", "eligible overseas
-- representative"; ss 6, 6A, 7), when a Medicare benefit is payable for a professional service (s 10(1), (1A); s 17(1)(a);
-- s 19(1)-(6)), how much it is (s 9; s 10(2)-(5); s 14(1)), who it is paid to and what bulk billing is (s 20(1); s 20A(1)),
-- and the bar on charging a public patient for a public hospital service (s 3(1) "public hospital service", "public patient",
-- "recognised hospital"; s 128C).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 136, compilation date 19 September 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 90, 2026), register id
-- C2026C00411, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00101.txt.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0008 in subjects/au/requirements.jsonl (priority 1), raised 7 times by the three Western
-- Australian cradle-to-grave scenarios (Chloe c002, c060, c065; Jake k003, k044, k090; Daniel d002). SCOPED to the provisions
-- and questions those events name -- is a newborn eligible; what is bulk-billed and what does a public patient pay; what does
-- Medicare cover after a stroke; treatment after a road injury -- with the definitions, conditions and exceptions needed to
-- answer them.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. The Medicare Benefits Schedule itself (the "table" of items and Schedule fees is made by regulation and was not
-- deposited: every Schedule fee is an INPUT, and so is whether a service is "prescribed" for the 100% rate under s 10(2)(aa));
-- whether a service is a "professional service" (an item relating to it, and "clinically relevant") is an INPUT; the safety
-- nets (ss 10AA-10AE, 10ACA, 10ADA) and indexation (s 10A); the multiple-operation, anaesthesia, pathology, diagnostic imaging
-- and radiation oncology rules (ss 15-16G); practitioner-side bars (ss 19AA-19C, the My Health Record rules in ss 19AD-19AI);
-- simplified billing (s 20A(2), s 20AAA); claims (s 20B); Parts IIA onwards except s 128C. The regulations that s 6A, s 20A(1)(d)
-- and s 128C(1) rely on were not deposited: their effect is an INPUT. Recovery of Medicare benefits out of compensation or
-- damages (k044) is not in this Act at all (see NOTES.md).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Health Insurance Act 1973 -- Medicare`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `s 3(1) -- Australian resident; eligible person`

-- s 3(1): "Australian resident means a person who resides in Australia and who is: (a) an Australian citizen; or (b) ... the
-- holder of a permanent visa; or (ba) a person who has been granted, or who is included in, a return endorsement or a resident
-- return visa ...; or (c) a New Zealand citizen who is lawfully present in Australia; or (d) a person ... who is lawfully present
-- in Australia and whose continued presence in Australia is not subject to any limitation as to time imposed by law; or (f) a
-- person who: (i) is ... the holder of a temporary visa; and (ia) is not covered by regulations made under subsection 6A(1); and
-- (ii) has applied for a permanent visa ... and the application has not been withdrawn or otherwise finally determined; and (iii)
-- has not, both: (A) ... made an application for a protection visa ... [still pending]; and (B) ... made an application for a
-- parent visa ...; and (iv) has not ... made an application for a parent visa ... [still pending]; and (v) in respect of whom
-- either: (A) another person, being the person's spouse, parent or child ..., is an Australian citizen or the holder of a
-- permanent visa ...; or (B) an authority to work in Australia is in force." (There is no paragraph (e) in the deposit.)
-- "eligible person means an Australian resident or an eligible overseas representative."
-- There is no age condition and no enrolment condition: a newborn who is a citizen and resides in Australia is an eligible
-- person from birth. "medicare number" is defined only by reference to s 84(1) of the National Health Act 1953; the card and
-- enrolment are not in this Act.
--
-- s 6(1): the Minister may, by order, declare that a person who "would not be an eligible person" is to be treated as one.
-- s 6(2): by legislative instrument, that a person who "would be an eligible person" is to be treated as not one,
-- "notwithstanding anything in this Act". s 6A(1): regulations may treat a holder of a prescribed temporary visa as an eligible
-- person "while he or she is in Australia". s 7(2): a visitor covered by a reciprocal agreement "shall, subject to the agreement,
-- be treated as an eligible person ... during his or her stay in Australia".
DECLARE Person HAS
    `resides in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an Australian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a permanent visa` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a return endorsement or resident return visa` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a New Zealand citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is lawfully present in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `presence not limited in time by law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a temporary visa` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is covered by s 6A(1) regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a pending permanent visa application` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a pending protection visa application and has applied for a parent visa` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a pending parent visa application` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a spouse, parent or child who is a citizen or permanent visa holder` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has an authority to work in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an eligible overseas representative` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is declared eligible by a Ministerial order under s 6(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is declared not eligible by an order under s 6(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a reciprocal agreement visitor under s 7` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `p` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person comes within paragraph (f)` IF
        `p`'s `holds a temporary visa`
    AND (NOT `p`'s `is covered by s 6A(1) regulations`)
    AND `p`'s `has a pending permanent visa application`
    AND (NOT `p`'s `has a pending protection visa application and has applied for a parent visa`)
    AND (NOT `p`'s `has a pending parent visa application`)
    AND (    `p`'s `has a spouse, parent or child who is a citizen or permanent visa holder`
         OR  `p`'s `has an authority to work in Australia`)

GIVEN `p` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is an Australian resident` IF
        `p`'s `resides in Australia`
    AND (    `p`'s `is an Australian citizen`
         OR  `p`'s `holds a permanent visa`
         OR  `p`'s `has a return endorsement or resident return visa`
         OR  (`p`'s `is a New Zealand citizen` AND `p`'s `is lawfully present in Australia`)
         OR  (`p`'s `is lawfully present in Australia` AND `p`'s `presence not limited in time by law`)
         OR  `the person comes within paragraph (f)` `p`)

GIVEN `p` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is an eligible person` IF
        (    `the person is an Australian resident` `p`
         OR  `p`'s `is an eligible overseas representative`
         OR  `p`'s `is declared eligible by a Ministerial order under s 6(1)`
         OR  `p`'s `is covered by s 6A(1) regulations`
         OR  `p`'s `is a reciprocal agreement visitor under s 7`)
    AND (NOT `p`'s `is declared not eligible by an order under s 6(2)`)

§§ `ss 10(1), 17, 19 -- when a Medicare benefit is payable`

-- s 10(1): "Where, on or after 1 February 1984, medical expenses are incurred in respect of a professional service rendered in
-- Australia to an eligible person, medicare benefit calculated in accordance with subsection (2) is payable". (1A): a service on
-- a "domestic journey" is taken to be rendered in Australia.
-- s 17(1): a medicare benefit "is not payable" if "(a) the medical expenses in respect of that service have been paid, or are
-- payable, to a recognized hospital" (paras (b)-(d) -- prescribed organisations and s 42B schemes -- are not encoded).
-- s 19(1): not payable for a medical examination for "(a) life insurance; (b) superannuation or provident account schemes; or (c)
-- admission to membership of a friendly society". (2) "Unless the Minister otherwise directs", not payable for a service
-- rendered "by, or on behalf of, or under an arrangement with: (a) the Commonwealth; (b) a State; (c) a local governing body; or
-- (d) an authority established by a law" of the Commonwealth, a State or an internal Territory. (3) "Unless the Minister
-- otherwise directs", not payable if "(a) the medical expenses ... were incurred by the employer" (para (b), industrial
-- undertakings, is not encoded). (4) not payable for a service "rendered in the course of the carrying out of a mass
-- immunization". (5) "Unless the Minister otherwise directs", not payable for "a health screening service". (6) not payable
-- unless the prescribed particulars have been recorded on the account or receipt.
-- ENCODING CHOICE: one flag stands for a Ministerial direction disapplying whichever of s 19(2), (3), (5) is engaged.
DECLARE Service HAS
    `the patient` IS A Person
    `date rendered as YYYYMMDD` IS A NUMBER
    `rendered in Australia or on a domestic journey` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a professional service` IS A BOOLEAN
    `medical expenses incurred` IS A BOOLEAN
    `expenses paid or payable to a recognised hospital` IS A BOOLEAN
    `rendered by or for the Commonwealth, a State, a local body or a statutory authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `expenses incurred by the patient's employer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a health screening service` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister has directed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an examination for life insurance, superannuation or a friendly society` IS A BOOLEAN
    `rendered in a mass immunisation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `prescribed particulars recorded` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `s` IS A Service
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a Medicare benefit is payable for the service` IF
        `s`'s `date rendered as YYYYMMDD` AT LEAST 19840201
    AND `s`'s `rendered in Australia or on a domestic journey`
    AND `the person is an eligible person` (`s`'s `the patient`)
    AND `s`'s `is a professional service`
    AND `s`'s `medical expenses incurred`
    AND (NOT `s`'s `expenses paid or payable to a recognised hospital`)
    AND (NOT `s`'s `is an examination for life insurance, superannuation or a friendly society`)
    AND (NOT `s`'s `rendered in a mass immunisation`)
    AND (    `s`'s `the Minister has directed otherwise`
         OR  (    (NOT `s`'s `rendered by or for the Commonwealth, a State, a local body or a statutory authority`)
              AND (NOT `s`'s `expenses incurred by the patient's employer`)
              AND (NOT `s`'s `is a health screening service`)))
    AND `s`'s `prescribed particulars recorded`

§§ `ss 9, 10(2)-(5), 14 -- how much`

-- s 9: benefits "shall be calculated by reference to the fees for medical services set out in the table".
-- s 10(2): "A benefit in respect of a service is: (a) in the case of a service provided: (i) as part of an episode of hospital
-- treatment; or (ii) as part of an episode of hospital-substitute treatment in respect of which the person ... chooses to receive
-- a benefit from a private health insurer; an amount equal to 75% of the Schedule fee; or (aa) in the case of a service to which
-- paragraph (a) does not apply and that is prescribed by the regulations ...--an amount equal to 100% of the Schedule fee; or (b)
-- in any other case--an amount equal to 85% of the Schedule fee."
-- (3): "If the Schedule fee exceeds the amount of benefit calculated under paragraph (2)(b) by more than the greatest permissible
-- gap, the benefit is taken to be the Schedule fee less the greatest permissible gap." (5): "greatest permissible gap means
-- $50.00." (4): an amount "not a multiple of 5 cents ... is to be rounded up to the nearest multiple of 5 cents".
-- s 14(1): a benefit "shall not exceed the medical expenses incurred" ((2), insurer agreements not on a fee-for-service basis,
-- is not encoded).
-- ENCODING CHOICE: the 5-cent rounding in (4) is applied to the (2) amount before the (3) comparison; with Schedule fees that are
-- whole multiples of 5 cents the order makes no difference.
DECLARE ServiceSetting IS ONE OF
    `outside any episode of hospital treatment`
    `part of an episode of hospital treatment`
    `hospital-substitute treatment with a private insurer benefit chosen`
    `hospital-substitute treatment with no private insurer benefit chosen`

GIVEN `the setting` IS A ServiceSetting, `prescribed for the 100 per cent rate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the benefit percentage` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the setting`
    WHEN `part of an episode of hospital treatment` THEN 75
    WHEN `hospital-substitute treatment with a private insurer benefit chosen` THEN 75
    OTHERWISE IF `prescribed for the 100 per cent rate` THEN 100 ELSE 85

`the greatest permissible gap` MEANS 50

GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded up to 5 cents` MEANS
    (0 MINUS FLOOR (0 MINUS (`x` TIMES 20))) DIVIDED BY 20

GIVEN `the Schedule fee` IS A NUMBER, `the setting` IS A ServiceSetting, `prescribed for the 100 per cent rate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the benefit under s 10` MEANS
    IF      `the benefit percentage` `the setting` `prescribed for the 100 per cent rate` EQUALS 85
        AND `the Schedule fee` MINUS `the calculated amount` GREATER THAN `the greatest permissible gap`
    THEN `the Schedule fee` MINUS `the greatest permissible gap`
    ELSE `the calculated amount`
    WHERE
        `the calculated amount` MEANS
            `rounded up to 5 cents`
                (`the Schedule fee` TIMES `the benefit percentage` `the setting` `prescribed for the 100 per cent rate` DIVIDED BY 100)

GIVEN `the Schedule fee` IS A NUMBER, `the setting` IS A ServiceSetting, `prescribed for the 100 per cent rate` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the medical expenses` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Medicare benefit` MEANS
    `the lesser of` (`the benefit under s 10` `the Schedule fee` `the setting` `prescribed for the 100 per cent rate`)
                    `the medical expenses`

§§ `ss 20(1), 20A(1) -- who is paid; bulk billing`

-- s 20(1): the benefit "is payable ... to the person who incurs the medical expenses in respect of that service". (2): if that
-- person has not paid, he or she is not paid the benefit but may ask for a cheque drawn in favour of the practitioner.
-- s 20A(1) ("Bulk billing assignments"): an eligible person "may enter into an agreement to assign the assignor's right to the
-- payment of the medicare benefit if: (a) the professional service is or will be rendered to the assignor or to another eligible
-- person; and (b) the agreement is entered into with the person by whom, or on whose behalf, the professional service is or will
-- be rendered (the professional); and (c) the agreement provides that: (i) the assignor assigns ... ; and (ii) the professional
-- accepts the assignment in full payment of the medical expenses ...; and (d) any requirements specified in the regulations are
-- met." (5): "An assignment of a medicare benefit shall not be made except in accordance with this section."
-- READING (an inference from (c)(ii)): once a valid bulk-billing assignment is made, the patient owes nothing for the service.
GIVEN `the assignor is an eligible person` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the service is rendered to an eligible person` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the agreement is with the professional` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the professional accepts the assignment in full payment` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the regulation requirements are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the bulk-billing assignment is valid` IF
        `the assignor is an eligible person`
    AND `the service is rendered to an eligible person`
    AND `the agreement is with the professional`
    AND `the professional accepts the assignment in full payment`
    AND `the regulation requirements are met`

GIVEN `the fee charged` IS A NUMBER, `the benefit` IS A NUMBER, `bulk billed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the patient's out-of-pocket amount` MEANS
    IF `bulk billed` THEN 0 ELSE `the greater of` 0 (`the fee charged` MINUS `the benefit`)

§§ `ss 3(1), 128C -- public patients in public hospitals`

-- s 3(1): "public hospital service means a hospital service provided in: (a) a recognised hospital; or (b) a hospital in respect
-- of which the Commonwealth, or a State, provides funding for the provision of hospital services to public patients." "public
-- patient ... means a patient in respect of whom the hospital provides comprehensive care, including all necessary medical,
-- nursing and diagnostic services ...". "recognised hospital" is one with a statement under s 121-5(8) of the Private Health
-- Insurance Act 2007 that it is a public hospital.
-- s 128C(1): "A person mentioned in subsection (2) must not, in circumstances set out in the regulations: (a) charge a fee for the
-- provision of a public hospital service; or (b) receive any payment or other consideration from anyone in respect of the
-- provision of a public hospital service; if the person knows that the person to whom the service is ... provided is, or
-- intends to be, a public patient in the hospital. Penalty: 50 penalty units." (2): "(a) a medical practitioner; (b) a
-- participating midwife; (c) a participating nurse practitioner; (d) a person acting on behalf of" one of them.
-- The hospital itself is not in the list: what the hospital charges a public patient is not answered by this Act.
DECLARE Charger IS ONE OF
    `a medical practitioner`
    `a participating midwife`
    `a participating nurse practitioner`
    `a person acting on behalf of a practitioner, midwife or nurse practitioner`
    `the hospital itself`

GIVEN `in a recognised hospital` IS A BOOLEAN, `in a hospital publicly funded for public patients` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the service is a public hospital service` IF
    `in a recognised hospital` OR `in a hospital publicly funded for public patients`

GIVEN `the charger` IS A Charger,
      `in a recognised hospital` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `in a hospital publicly funded for public patients` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knows the patient is or intends to be a public patient` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the regulations' circumstances apply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `charging for the service contravenes s 128C` IF
        `the service is a public hospital service` `in a recognised hospital` `in a hospital publicly funded for public patients`
    AND `knows the patient is or intends to be a public patient`
    AND `the regulations' circumstances apply`
    AND CONSIDER `the charger`
        WHEN `the hospital itself` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

`the maximum penalty for charging a public patient in penalty units` MEANS 50
